WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.067
The United States has now

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:03.303
surpassed more than 150 mass shootings

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:03.670
this year.

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:04.671
That's according to the Gun

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:06.106
Violence Archive.

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:07.774
CNN defines a mass shooting as one in

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:09.476
which at least four people are shot,

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:11.611
not including the shooter.

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:12.812
Four such instances

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:13.346
were reported

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:15.048
yesterday in New York City, in Houston,

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:16.649
Detroit, in Bridgeport, Connecticut.

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:17.984
With each of these incidents

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:20.020
resulting in four victims

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:21.654
all told, more than 5000

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:23.089
people have been killed from gun violence

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:25.558
this year, including 73 children.

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:27.093
Relatedly, in our Politics

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:28.695
Lead, the National Rifle Association,

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:30.764
which continues to successfully lobby

00:00:30.764 --> 00:00:31.431
against gun

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:32.499
restrictions, ones

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:33.566
that are supported in polling

00:00:33.566 --> 00:00:34.801
by most Americans,

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.569
